    "difficulty": "Foundation",
    "difficultyReason": "There is one blank and a given trial (+) that is already ruled out. The student tests the remaining operations (×, −, ÷) on 3/4 and 1/2 and checks each result against 3/2. Each test is a single direct fraction calculation, and spotting that dividing by 1/2 doubles the number is the only interpretive step. This is a little harder than the direct decimal-multiplication practice in p88-q10, because the student must choose between operations and test them. It is easier than p96-q4, which needs a formula, a diagram reading and mixed-number conversion. It has none of the order-of-operations or multi-blank search of p97-q8.",
